From bcd414a5488018f304d9d741107617b5ba041b23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:54:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: every text of the player information fits its row,
 in English and in Spanish
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The labels of the player information neither wrap (but those made to) nor scroll, so a
text wider than its label is cut. Every label and button of its pages (the panel as Hades
makes it for every skin, system/hades/DialogHadesPlayerInfo.xml) was measured with
Estuary's fonts at the size of each control, with the widest text it can show: the
widest value of each variable and map, the widest sample of the properties that the
window system publishes, long values of Kodi's labels (the HDR detail of a profile 7 with
its FEL, "Portuguese (Brazil)", DTS-HD MA with DTS:X IMAX, the dialogue levels). 26 of
them in English and 29 to 31 in Spanish did not fit, and the label of the video scaling
method with the note of Hades did not fit the setting in Spanish.

Where the name of a row is short, the value takes the room it needs (the RPU, the trims,
the format with its HDR detail, the signalling, the framebuffer, the link, the subtitles,
the dialogue levels, what the TV offers, the GPU per pass); where the value is short, the
name does (MaxCLL / MaxFALL, the HDR10+ rows, L5 sent, the subtitle and audio decoders).
Some values take the smaller font of their neighbours (the codec, the layers, the GPU).
The sound as it is sent (with its reason) and the fidelity step-down take two lines
(HadesPanelRowText), the menus in Dolby Vision a line of their own; the transport of Dolby
Vision keeps its one line (with two, the last row of the left column of the Dolby Vision
page, 440 px high, would be pushed out of it where HDMI 1.4b signalling is shown). The sound on the overview says "PCM, decoded" without its reason, which the heading
says and the audio page in full (HadesOvAudioOutVar).

Texts said in fewer words, with the same sense: the RPU measured where the output takes no
HDR10, and the one converted from HLG; "Ordinary, no Dolby Vision"; "8-bit RGB set in the
settings"; "L5 sent (with the overlays)"; "DV Standard, HDMI 1.4b signalling" and "DV
without the Standard mode"; "Low-Latency, mapped by Hades (4:2:2, 12 bits)"; the
transport converted to BT.2020 as a "fallback for this video"; "simpler rounding under
the GUI"; in Spanish also the HDMI 1.4b InfoFrame, the colour of
IPT-PQ-c2, "El vídeo no tiene metadatos HDR ni Dolby Vision." and the note of the video
scaling method, "(no lo usa Dolby Vision)". The msgid of the Spanish files is the new
English. system/hades is made again by make-playerinfo.py.

Looked at in Kodi itself, in QEMU with screenshots (with one more set of samples: the longest heading, PCM decoded with its
reason): the pages in English and Spanish, the heading with the longest reason, the table
of the levels with its legend.

Host test (outside the tree): measure_all.py, in en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx: 118
controls that do not fit before (with the note of the video scaling method), none after.
The heading and the reasons (measure.py), the checks of the skin of the player information (validate_skin.py, validate_hades_dialog.py), make-playerinfo.py --check and the checks
of the strings (msgidsync.py, maptest.py, po-dups.py) pass.
